---
description: Security, validation, and data-write rules
alwaysApply: true
---

# Secrets

- Never hard-code secrets. Read them from environment variables.
- Never expose the Supabase service role key to the browser. Use it only in server code.

# Validation and writes

- Validate ALL user input on the server with Zod, even when the browser already validates it.
- Use Server Actions or Route Handlers for anything that writes data. Do not write from client-only code.

# Supabase

- Enable Row Level Security on every table.
- Write explicit policies for each table (who can select, insert, update, delete).
